# 1v1, CassiusClay shielded with a 0.4 power floor on fresh PC seeds (BENCH-235, SHIELD-25,
# docs/bench/local/2026-11-09_view-rank.md, "R1 recheck and the power floor"). Leigh starts it once the PC is free
# (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-shield-floor        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-shield-floor)
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned, 12 workers, truth log off. Every step resumes; no step needs a
# decision. About 15 minutes of battles (1 robot x 4 arms x 12 seeds = 48; shielded rounds run long).
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: every line names CassiusClay; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master.
#   - CassiusClay is the largest gap left on the field ledger's R1 route (master 60.1 against BeepBoop's 95.5 on the
#     cloud R1 recheck). BeepBoop stands still and shields it, takes 0.6 damage a round, and CassiusClay drains itself to
#     0 energy firing 1.9 to 2.6 power.
#   - The mechanism is in CassiusClay's published source (pgun/Bee.java): when the enemy's last bullet was under 0.4
#     power it fires that power back. Our shield fires 0.1 interceptors, so it gets 0.1 bullets in return, cheap for it,
#     and rounds run to 3,000 ticks; list + still alone reads -1.2 on the cloud.
#   - Cloud screen (6 seeds from 14400): list + still + floor +40.4 (low end +36.6) over master, 98.8 against
#     BeepBoop's 98.0; damage taken 29.7 -> 0.7 a round.
#   - Risk: the floor loses heavily on robots that bait with 0.1 bullets rather than copy (CobraBora -75.7, MatchupMicro
#     -79.9, PastFuture -15.4) and gains on none of the 11 other field jars with the same copy-power field, so it ships
#     for CassiusClay alone, at a 3-point margin with its 95% low end above 0.
# gate: the per-robot pick (`mode_table.py --margin 3`, interval above 0) names the line to ship; a one-robot card has
# no cross-robot APS gate. No pilot or futility rule: one robot is too few for an interim read.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): halt on 30 failed battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle
# over the last 200, or no battle in 30 minutes; every battle fought is kept and a rerun resumes. ALERT opens an
# issue for Leigh on any stop. Nothing here ships: on a pass a PR adds the held lines to ShieldListData,
# ShieldTableData.stills() and ShieldTableData.shieldFloors() for the next release.

set V = 3.22
set P = --parallel 12 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant 1488498 --child-heap 2G
set W = work/shield-floor-pc
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && SHIELD_ADD=plans/shield-floor-add.txt SHIELD_STILL=plans/shield-floor-add.txt bash ./build-ablation.sh slistadd,szlist && SHIELD_ADD=plans/shield-floor-add.txt SHIELD_STILL=plans/shield-floor-add.txt SHIELD_FLOOR=plans/shield-floor-add.txt bash ./build-ablation.sh slistadd,szlist,sfloorlist && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}mtzl.jar && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}mtzlsf.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-shield-floor.txt && mvn -q compile

confirm | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-shield-floor.txt --seeds 12 --seed-base 14800 --arms plans/pc-shield-floor.arms --out ${W} --label shield-floor-pc --shuffle-jobs
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 200
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_shield-floor-pc.md && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms.tsv --margin 3 --out-tsv ${OUT}/shield-floor-pc-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_shield-floor-pc-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms.tsv --arms mz sf --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_shield-floor-pc-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/shield-floor-pc-per-robot.tsv
  after: confirm

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-shield-floor-results "1v1 CassiusClay shielded with a 0.4 power floor, 12 fresh seeds" ${OUT}/*_shield-floor-pc*.md ${OUT}/shield-floor-pc-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name shield-floor-pc-pick.tsv -size +0c)
  after: gate
